WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.590
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.210
I’ll be the one to defeat Playmaker!

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.330
You have a grudge against him?

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.730
He’s always ahead of me.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.740
Let’s battle, Playmaker!

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.500
Playmaker, will you let me handle this?

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.570
Okay.  I leave this to you.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.760
Emerald Overload!

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.620
Go Onizuka!

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.990
For me, you're the hero who defeated 
the Hanoi and saved LINK VRAINS.

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:41.380
Listen, I'll tell you this.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:44.990
No one can always win.

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:47.500
Everyone experiences defeat.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.530
Will defeat rot you?  Or will 
you use it as a springboard?

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.630
When you lose, the true you is revealed!

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:02.940
I've caught the bounty.

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:25.280
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:32.060
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:39.370
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:45.940
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:52.680
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:59.920
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:06.630
I want to share your pain

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:44.690
Hey!  He’s shooting!

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:45.940
I know!

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.020
I'll use my secret weapon!

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.390
Release the Data Storm!

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:00.290
I’ll chase you away like last time-

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.770
I’m sorry!

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:07.960
Yusaku, can you hear me?

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:09.870
I’m in the middle of something!

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:14.900
Even for the restricted area, 
your location is very unstable.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:18.260
If you get too far from the 
center, you can't come back.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.660
And if I can't?

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.580
You’ll drown in data.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:24.920
He'll destroys us before then!

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.550
Calm down!  He’s trying to intimidate us!

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:32.190
Unless he wins a duel, he can’t take you!

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:38.260
I’ll count to three.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:43.100
Surrender or duel.  Decide.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.630
He’s letting us decide.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.080
What a nice guy!

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.700
One.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.250
What will you do, Playmaker?

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.150
Two.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.410
Wait a sec!

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.960
You only counted to two!

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.260
I see.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.960
You're OK with that?

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:13.340
Since he said three, he made us 
think he’ll wait until three.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:18.340
So if he surprise attacks at two, we’ll 
let our guard down for one count.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:19.810
I see!

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:23.380
He’s willing to do anything 
to fulfill his goal.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:30.390
Beyond those security cameras 
is the restricted area.

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.750
The surveillance is tight.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.100
No need to worry.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.790
As long as you wear my stealth program.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.490
But this data is heavy.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.150
Oh, sorry.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.740
Let’s go.

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.710
Wow, Ghost Girl.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:54.970
She's skilled at sneaking.

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:56.720
Is that a compliment?

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:57.750
Of course.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:02.220
If my brother can count 
on you, I can admire you.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.020
Thank you.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:07.260
Six Ignis?

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.330
That’s right.

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:11.100
The Lost Incident created the Ignis.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.260
One of them is Playmaker’s AI.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:18.360
The six created their own 
world - Cyberse World.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:22.840
But someone destroyed it, scattering them.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:27.040
Emma, I want you to find the other Ignis.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:32.450
But didn't you hire infamous 
bounty hunters to find them?

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.620
You want to keep this 
secret from your company.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.780
Look at this.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:49.200
The other day, someone battled Playmaker 
and vanished into the restricted area.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:53.850
There’s a mysterious gate in the 
restricted area's lowest section.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:57.940
It probably connects to an unknown world.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:02.350
Whoever battled Playmaker 
must have went there.

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:06.510
A few days ago, we sent a 
research team to that gate.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:07.820
The result?

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:10.820
Not a single one returned.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:15.170
The Ignis may be hiding there.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:17.620
This is a dangerous task.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:19.750
I can only rely on you.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.830
Why do you want the Ignis so badly?

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:26.210
Planning to get them before 
your company and negotiate?

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:29.020
My brother isn’t like that!

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:32.470
Ignis are a threat to humans.  However…

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:34.210
However?

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.320
What's their intention?

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:38.680
Do they view humans as the enemy?

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:41.180
I want to learn the truth.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:46.220
Payment is three times the usual.

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:49.540
If you're keeping this a 
secret from your company...

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:52.830
...your hunters will hunt me if I mess up.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.200
Including Blood Shepherd.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:02.140
That’s plenty of risk to ask 
for three times the usual.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:05.130
Understood.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:07.810
Okay.  Negotiations complete.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:10.720
Let me give you this.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.810
What is it?

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:16.520
A program that forces you 
to log out.  Just in case.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:20.220
It can only be used once, but 
it'll give you peace of mind.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:23.220
What an undependable present.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.770
Downloaded transfer data.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.230
Well, I’ll take it for peace of mind-

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:30.840
Downloaded transfer data.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:36.440
Akira!  She’s not ready yet!

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:37.620
It’s too dangerous!

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.650
No, I’m going.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:41.520
Please let me go!

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.080
You’ll drag me down!

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:47.250
I'll protect myself.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:51.820
I'll fight so that you can learn the truth!

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.440
Aoi…

00:07:57.650 --> 00:08:00.780
But take this to heart:

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.950
Humanity's future rests on this mission.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:04.670
Yes.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.380
And…

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:09.100
You must return safely.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.380
Brother…

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:18.580
Communication between us 
will be completely cut.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:22.520
If you get in trouble, I 
won’t be able to help.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:26.500
I know.  We're responsible for ourselves.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.350
Good luck.

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:32.880
Ready?

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:34.060
Yes.

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:36.230
Into the VRAINS!

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.860
It’s quiet.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:46.550
The bounty hunters aren’t here.

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:48.020
Of course not.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:51.660
They went to the lowest level 
to chase after Playmaker.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:53.560
What do you mean?

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:57.900
I sent Playmaker info about the 
restricted area and the gate.

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:01.120
Along with how to get past security.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.090
Why?

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:06.820
To draw the hunters away, of course.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:09.330
Always best to minimize risk.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:11.570
You used Playmaker?

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:16.560
He's also using my info, 
so it's an equal exchange.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:23.580
Okay.  We passed the heavy surveillance.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.820
Remove stealth.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.860
This data truly was heavy.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:46.300
You look quite mature.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:50.110
I can’t wear my usual 
outfit for a secret mission.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:55.060
Then you've updated from 
Blue Angel to Blue Girl.

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:57.340
Thanks for the name.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:02.760
You seemed worried about 
the hunter, Blood Shepherd.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:04.290
He’s trouble.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:07.020
Once he’s after you, he 
won’t let you escape.

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:09.760
No matter what it takes.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:11.500
He’s so persistent!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:14.030
It seems we’ll have to battle.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:17.540
He's not surrendering.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:18.670
In that case…

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:21.900
I’ll take your Ignis!

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:24.200
Speed Duel!

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:33.910
I’ll go first.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:35.470
My turn!

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:38.560
I summon Drone Pawn from my hand.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:41.940
600 ATK?

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:47.520
Since he knows he's facing Playmaker, 
he must be up to something.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:48.600
Be quiet!

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:49.540
Okay.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:52.840
I set one card and end my turn.

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:55.820
Done already?

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:57.940
Hey, Playmaker.

00:10:57.940 --> 00:11:00.310
Maybe he’s bad at dueling.

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:04.280
That’s why he bluffed by shooting at us.

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:06.280
Drone Pawn’s effect.

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:11.990
When no other monsters are on our field, 
it can’t be destroyed in battle.

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:16.140
And during the turn that it's 
attacked, after the battle...

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:19.030
...we regain LP equal to the damage we took.

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:22.340
That AI talks a lot!

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:24.210
I'll take 'em on!

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:27.020
Be quiet.  Don’t interfere.

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:28.040
Okay.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:32.720
Checking his past duels, 
anything to focus on?

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:37.750
Be careful of the new Link Monster 
he summoned in his last duel.

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:43.460
Its consecutive attacks 
defeated his opponent.

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:46.450
If Playmaker successfully summons it...

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:51.600
...Drone Pawn is in position to activate 
his consecutive attack effect.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:57.330
I should've checked before 
summoning Drone Pawn.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:02.040
That AI’s info is correct!

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:06.000
In other words, you’re going to lose!

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.310
Be quiet.

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:10.700
Even the enemy said it.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:13.970
You know Blood Shepherd?

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:17.460
Yes.  Your brother does too.

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:21.290
A job three years ago.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:32.370
We were chasing an evil hacker in a 
net world different from LINK VRAINS.

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:34.530
Stay back!

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:40.080
Come any closer, I’ll 
blow you up with this!

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:44.480
He changed a hacking program into a bomb!

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:49.520
If you're hit with this, you'll take 
a lot of damage in the real world too!

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:51.600
This is bad.

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:54.600
There'll be consequences if we're hit.  So...

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:56.060
Count to three.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:57.310
What?

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.530
I don’t care for a long battle.

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:03.220
We'll all charge at the count of three.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.560
But…

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:08.460
Three!  Surrender before then!

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:12.280
Stop joking!  Don’t you see what I have-

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:18.340
One.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:20.610
Damn!  He’s serious!

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.040
Guess we're doing this.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:23.750
Seems so.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:26.420
Two.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.290
Three.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:34.030
What?

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:35.670
Damn!

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.130
Spider web?

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:05.460
He planned to use us as 
decoys from the start.

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:08.230
Watch out!  Ghost Girl, above!

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:12.400
Damn!

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.310
I'll destroy the bomb program.

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:18.140
Move, Emma!

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:46.420
Are you okay, Ghost Girl?

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:47.740
Yeah.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.380
You…

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:52.510
You tricked us and used us as decoys!

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:58.650
Mission complete.

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:01.180
Any more is a waste of time.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:03.450
Wait!

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:08.020
Damn!  What’s he thinking?

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:12.940
He called me Emma…

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.480
What’s wrong?

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:19.580
You're suddenly quiet.

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:21.350
It’s nothing.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:25.840
Anyway, Blood Shepherd will do 
anything to fulfill his mission.

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:27.550
He’s dangerous.

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:32.270
What if someone loses to him?

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:37.080
Playmaker’s Ignis will 
go to SOL Technologies.

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:44.090
Kusanagi, there’s a 
hole ahead I can go down.

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:47.100
The corridors ahead are like floors.

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:51.420
Go down the hole and you're 
closer to the center.

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:52.800
Okay.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.020
When you're through, turn around.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:01.640
There's another hole that 
leads to the center.

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:05.240
Oh yeah!

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:08.880
Full throttle, Playmaker!

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:11.450
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:14.690
I summon Clock Wyvern!

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:21.370
When it's summoned, its effect activates!

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:26.280
By halving its ATK, I Special 
Summon a Clock Token!

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.340
We’re not done!

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:31.620
When there’s a Cyberse on my field...

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:35.810
...I can Special Summon this 
card from my hand once per turn!

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:39.040
Come, Backup Secretary!

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:43.250
Do the usual thing!

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:45.540
The circuit that leads to the future!

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:49.950
The summoning conditions are 
two Level 3 or higher Cyberses!

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.690
Link Summon!

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:55.400
Appear, Link 2 Elphase!

00:16:56.930 --> 00:16:59.970
We’re not done!

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:03.230
Huh?  What’s wrong, Playmaker?

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:06.360
The set card can’t be activated.

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:07.380
Be quiet.

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:10.840
We can’t waste time on this guy!

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.940
Let’s defeat him quick!

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:14.320
Appear again!

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:16.320
The circuit that leads to the future!

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:20.060
The summoning conditions 
are at least two Cyberses!

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:25.030
I set Clock Token and Link 2 
Elphase in the Link Markers!

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:27.870
Link Summon!

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:33.580
Appear, Link 3 Shootingcode Talker!

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:37.770
That’s what I was waiting for!

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:45.250
The headliner - Shootingcode 
Talker - has appeared!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:52.990
In addition to its usual attack, it gains an 
attack for every monster next to its link.

00:17:52.990 --> 00:18:01.420
But when you only have one monster when 
this effect is used, it loses 400 ATK.

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:08.870
The damage from Shootingcode Talker and 
Drone Pawn’s battle will be reduced to 1300.

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:10.500
Correct!

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:14.420
Currently, Shootingcode 
Talker can attack twice.

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:17.980
Therefore, we will take 2600 damage.

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:22.680
But due to Drone Pawn’s effect, 
our LP will regain all that damage.

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:24.230
But wait!

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:26.620
We’re not done yet!

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.620
Elphase’s effect!

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.620
When it's Link Summoned 
and leaves the field...

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:37.470
...I can Special Summon a Level 4 
or lower Cyberse from my graveyard!

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:40.800
Come, Clock Wyvern!

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:46.280
A second monster was summoned next 
to Shootingcode Talker’s link.

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:49.270
Now it can attack three times.

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:51.440
We will have 100 LP left.

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:55.260
Then if Clock Wyvern 
attacks, we'll have 0 LP.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:56.690
Ding ding ding!

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.250
Correct, AI!

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:01.020
What an easy win.

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:02.860
I was waiting for this.

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:05.790
I misled you so easily.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:06.930
Huh?

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:12.060
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Capture Drone!

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:17.120
I can activate it when 
there’s a Drone monster.

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:23.480
Your Link Monster can’t attack 
and has its effects negated.

00:19:24.110 --> 00:19:26.440
What?

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:34.210
It also can’t be used to 
Link Summon or be tributed!

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:38.490
Your AI said your set card couldn't activate!

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:40.990
It’s not that it couldn't activate.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:43.320
It’s that I didn’t activate it.

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:45.600
That’s not what it said!

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:49.880
Who decided that an AI's info is accurate?

00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:53.240
You made the AI tell a lie?

00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:54.530
Exactly.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:56.640
That’s cheating!

00:19:56.640 --> 00:20:00.920
You’re dumb for believing an AI’s info.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:04.690
Hey!  The one who says dumb is the dumb one!

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:09.540
AIs are never to be trusted.

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:11.100
What?

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:14.180
It seems you thoroughly analyzed my deck.

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:15.520
Of course.

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:19.070
Playmaker, you can’t defeat me.

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:23.700
I set one card and end my turn.

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:27.000
My turn.  I draw!

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:30.140
Come out!  The circuit that leads to victory!

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:32.110
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:20:32.110 --> 00:20:35.580
The summoning condition is one Drone!

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:37.500
Link Summon!

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.670
Link 1 Battledrone Sergeant!

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:47.480
Even if you sealed away our moves...

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:54.750
...your monster with 800 ATK can't destroy 
Shootingcode Talker with 2300 ATK.

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:58.450
You're bragging about 
info that I already know?

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:01.280
That AI truly is dumb.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:05.300
Like I said, the one who 
says dumb is the dumb one!

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:08.090
Capture Drone’s effect activates!

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:11.860
Once per turn, I can Special Summon Drone 
Tokens up to the number

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:14.710
of a target’s Link Markers.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:20.010
The target monster, Shootingcode 
Talker, has three Link Markers.

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:24.150
Be quiet.  I no longer have use for you.

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:28.300
I Special Summon three Drone 
Tokens in defense position!

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:31.860
Oh oh!  He has three to Link Summon!

00:21:31.860 --> 00:21:35.780
Come out again!  The circuit 
that leads to victory!

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:37.700
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:41.090
The summoning conditions 
are at least two Drones!

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:44.980
I set three Drone Tokens in the Link Markers!

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:48.190
Link Summon!

00:21:48.190 --> 00:21:50.040
Deploy!

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:55.230
Link 3 Battledrone General!

00:21:57.390 --> 00:21:59.840
A general?  This is terrible!

00:22:19.930 --> 00:22:26.240
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:32.950
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:36.450
Memories left behind  Erased memories

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:39.590
What was the PASSWORD again?

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.190
ACCESS records  Restored memories

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:47.160
Challenge "the you inside you"

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:58.040
You're a Network  The 
World that spreads beyond

00:22:58.200 --> 00:23:01.180
With repeating "nows"

00:23:01.530 --> 00:23:05.140
What about you?  "Live for now"

00:23:05.310 --> 00:23:11.090
Grab the Shooting Star in 
the sky with both your hands

00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:14.360
Overcome "now" with all your might  Yell!

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:41.890
The Battledrone has determined 
that Playmaker must be erased.

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:47.870
The sound it creates is far from natural.

00:23:47.870 --> 00:23:51.940
Emotionless and eerie.

00:23:51.940 --> 00:23:55.290
Like Blood Shepherd.

00:23:55.290 --> 00:23:58.720
He's trying to stop Storm Access.

00:23:58.720 --> 00:24:02.760
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Terrifying Battledrone

00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:04.930
Into the VRAINS!
